<title>SPAIN: Spain raises minimum wage by 2.6 percent.</title>
<headline>Spain raises minimum wage by 2.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government approved on Friday a rise in the minimum wage of 2.6 percent.</p>
<p>The increase is &quot;in line with government's inflation and wages targets and it respects the (EMU) convergence criteria,&quot; a Labour Ministry statement said.</p>
<p>For workers older than 18 years, the measure will bring a yearly increase in the wage of 66,630 pesetas. For workers younger than 18 years, the raise will be 17.73 pct or 59,130 pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
